Relief items were distributed during the operation based on immediate needs and requests on the ground (including from civil protection, citizens, and others in need of relief goods). Lunch packs and sandwiches were distributed to civil protection members, firefighters and other frontline workers, as well as to the affected population.

The operation covered 10 Red Cross units. RC branches carry different amounts of stock and consequently the number of items distributed also varies. Overall, 400 people were supported with relief supplies in the first hours of the emergency through the RCSBiH emergency response.
